1
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:04,840
(Leonard:)-Kites ho!
-Kites ho!

2
00:00:05,005 --> 00:00:06,255
(Leonard:)Kites ho!

3
00:00:06,423 --> 00:00:08,503
[IN UNISON]
Kites ho!

4
00:00:08,675 --> 00:00:11,845
(Sheldon:)Excuse me.
You're misusing the word "ho."

5
00:00:12,846 --> 00:00:16,556
(Sheldon:)It's an interjection used to call attention
to a destination, not an object.

6
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:20,355
As in, uh, "Land ho!"
or, uh, "Westward ho!"

7
00:00:22,856 --> 00:00:24,936
[IN UNISON]
Kites ho!

8
00:00:26,026 --> 00:00:27,816
Hey, guys. What are you doing?

9
00:00:27,986 --> 00:00:29,736
(Penny:)Going out to discover electricity?

10
00:00:29,904 --> 00:00:31,194
[CHUCKLES]

11
00:00:31,364 --> 00:00:35,204
If you refer to the work of Benjamin
Franklin, he did not discover electricity.

12
00:00:35,368 --> 00:00:38,958
(Leonard:)He merely used a kite to determine
that lightning consists of electricity.

13
00:00:39,122 --> 00:00:44,082
(Leonard:)He also invented the Franklin stove,
bifocals and the flexible urinary catheter.

14
00:00:46,796 --> 00:00:50,886
(Leonard:)-Kites ho.
-We're heading out for some kite fighting.

15
00:00:51,051 --> 00:00:52,681
(Penny:)-Kite fighting?
-Oh, yeah.

16
00:00:52,844 --> 00:00:56,094
(Leonard:)It's an extremely competitive,
cutthroat sport.

17
00:00:56,639 --> 00:00:59,929
(Sheldon:)Well, actually,
the risk of throat-cutting is very low.

18
00:01:00,101 --> 00:01:04,481
(Sheldon:)On the other hand, severe string burn
is a real and ever-present danger.

19
00:01:05,482 --> 00:01:09,982
-Uh, you wanna come watch?
-Oh, gee, ha, sounds amazing.

20
00:01:10,153 --> 00:01:12,153
(Penny:)But, um, I've got some friends
coming over.

21
00:01:12,322 --> 00:01:14,572
(Penny:)We're just gonna watch
the Nebraska game.

22
00:01:14,741 --> 00:01:16,871
(Leonard:)Oh, football, sure.

23
00:01:17,035 --> 00:01:18,865
(Howard:)Good guess.

24
00:01:20,830 --> 00:01:23,080
(Penny:)I would've invited you,
but you're not a fan.

25
00:01:23,249 --> 00:01:25,419
(Leonard:)No. No, I'm not. So, great.

26
00:01:25,794 --> 00:01:27,874
(Leonard:)You've got plans
doing something you like...

27
00:01:28,046 --> 00:01:30,716
(Leonard:)...I've got plans doing something I like,
so it's good.

28
00:01:30,882 --> 00:01:33,222
(Penny:)Maybe we'll hang out
after everybody's gone.

29
00:01:33,384 --> 00:01:36,674
(Leonard:)-Yeah, great.
-See you.

30
00:01:40,016 --> 00:01:41,846
(Leonard:)Well, this sucks.

31
00:01:43,061 --> 00:01:45,351
(Sheldon:)I'm sorry, I got bored and drifted off.

32
00:01:47,857 --> 00:01:51,147
(Sheldon:)Where exactly in the interaction
did the sucking lie?

33
00:01:51,778 --> 00:01:54,408
Leonard realized Penny's hiding him
from her friends...

34
00:01:54,572 --> 00:01:57,612
(Raj:)...because he's a tiny little man
who flies kites.

35
00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:03,040
(Sheldon:)Oh, that certainly would suck.

